  <!-- ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Tier C (design §3.2): one glyph per meme, chosen by affinity.
       GraffitiPool.MemeGateAllows only offers these to a placer whose Ideo
       holds the named meme (Ideo.HasMeme).

       Owner ruling 2026-09-24 (question card + free-text addition): "ALL
       vanilla memes get a mark, including Cannibal, MaleSupremacy/
       FemaleSupremacy, Nudism, Inhuman, PainIsVirtue - no exclusions."
       The mechanism (ModExtension_Graffiti.requiresAnyMeme + GraffitiPool's
       meme gate) already supports all 27 non-structure vanilla MemeDefs
       MEASURED this pass (`measure sql` on defs.sqlite, mods=623,
       captured=2026-09-24T00:30:55Z: 24 Ideology + Biotech Bloodfeeding +
       Anomaly Inhuman/Ritualist + Odyssey Shipborn). This file ships the
       EIGHT the owner's own ruling most needed proven - the six named
       explicitly (Cannibal/MaleSupremacy/FemaleSupremacy/Nudism/Inhuman/
       PainIsVirtue) plus two of the five placeholder-mapped memes this
       item's own open question left unresolved (Loyalist, Guilty) - rather
       than the pre-ruling design doc's own v1 shortlist (Raider/Cannibal/
       Supremacist/Collectivist/Individualist/Proselytizer/Transhumanist/
       NaturePrimacy), which conspicuously included none of the taste-
       boundary memes the ruling was actually about.

       Wave 2 (same item, this pass) ships the remaining 19: Raider,
       Blindsight, Darkness, Tunneler, Rancher, AnimalPersonhood,
       NaturePrimacy, TreeConnection, HumanPrimacy, Supremacist,
       Collectivist, Individualist, Proselytizer, Transhumanist,
       FleshPurity, HighLife, Bloodfeeding (Biotech), Ritualist (Anomaly),
       Shipborn (Odyssey) - all 27 non-structure ludeon.* MemeDefs now carry
       a glyph ThingDef.

       Glyph subjects are the design doc's own grounded readings (§3.2's
       table: each traced to the meme's description/style/precepts, not
       invented). Loyalist (banner) and Guilty (chain link) are explicitly
       PLACEHOLDER mappings per this item's open question 3 - flagged here,
       not settled. Wave 2 adds three more from that same open question:
       Collectivist, Individualist and Shipborn are ALSO placeholder
       subject mappings (linked rings / dot-in-ring / hull-and-star) -
       override when the owner has an image. Rancher/AnimalPersonhood and
       NaturePrimacy/TreeConnection were one table row apiece in the design
       doc's own §3.2 (it grouped them for exposition); each still gets its
       own single-meme ThingDef here so the 19-name accounting in this
       file's own wave-1 comment above resolves 1:1, not 17:2. -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="RM_BaseGraffiti" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">
    <defName>RM_Graffiti_Glyph_Cannibal</defName>
    <label>cannibal glyph</label>
    <description>A gnawed bone in a ring of toothmarks, wet from the brush - a mark for those who feed on their own kind.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <texPath>Things/Filth/Art/RM_Graffiti_Glyph_Cannibal</texPath>
      <drawSize>(1.25, 1)</drawSize>
      <shaderType>Mote</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Beauty>-6</Beauty>
      <Cleanliness>-3</Cleanliness>
    </statBases>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.Graffiti.ModExtension_Graffiti">
        <category>Taunt</category>
        <onViewOtherIdeo>RM_Graffiti_NearForeignSign</onViewOtherIdeo>
        <form>Glyph</form>
        <poolWeight>1</poolWeight>
        <raidExitEligible>true</raidExitEligible>
        <onViewHostileMaker>RM_Graffiti_ViewedHostileMark</onViewHostileMaker>
        <requiresAnyMeme>
          <li>Cannibal</li>
        </requiresAnyMeme>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

